    {
      "id": "q3",
      "number": 3,
      "type": "single",
      "topic": {
        "en": "Graph Theory",
        "zh": "图论"
      },
      "statement": {
        "en": "In creating a transportation network among the cities of Austin, Boston, Concord, Denver, and Frankford that uses the first letter of each city’s name, how many different routes (or simple paths) are there from Austin to Denver?\n\n{{diagram:elementary-q3-graph}}",
        "zh": "在 Austin、Boston、Concord、Denver 和 Frankford 之间建立如下交通网络，用各城市的首字母表示顶点。从 Austin 到 Denver 有多少条不同的路线（简单路径）？\n\n{{diagram:elementary-q3-graph}}"
      },
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": {
            "en": "4",
            "zh": "4"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": {
            "en": "5",
            "zh": "5"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": {
            "en": "6",
            "zh": "6"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": {
            "en": "7",
            "zh": "7"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "E",
          "text": {
            "en": "8",
            "zh": "8"
          }
        }
      ],
      "correctOptionIds": [
        "D"
      ],
      "explanation": {
        "en": "A simple path does not repeat a vertex. The 7 paths from A to D are AD, ACD, AFD, ABCD, ABFD, AFBCD and ACBFD. Answer D.",
        "zh": "答案：**D**。\n\n按从 A 出发的第一步分组，途中遇过的点不能再进。经 D 的只有 AD；经 C 有 ACD、ACBFD；经 F 有 AFD、AFBCD；经 B 有 ABCD、ABFD。共 $1+2+2+2=7$ 条。"
      },
