    {
      "id": "q4",
      "number": 4,
      "type": "single",
      "topic": {
        "en": "Graph Theory",
        "zh": "图论"
      },
      "statement": {
        "en": "In the undirected graph shown below that represents Al’s, Ben’s, Cy’s, Dave’s, and Eli’s houses using the first letter of each name, how many cycles are there?\n\n{{diagram:elementary-q4-graph}}",
        "zh": "下列无向图用姓名的首字母表示 Al、Ben、Cy、Dave 和 Eli 的房子。图中有多少个环？\n\n{{diagram:elementary-q4-graph}}"
      },
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": {
            "en": "4",
            "zh": "4"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": {
            "en": "6",
            "zh": "6"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": {
            "en": "8",
            "zh": "8"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": {
            "en": "10",
            "zh": "10"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "E",
          "text": {
            "en": "12",
            "zh": "12"
          }
        }
      ],
      "correctOptionIds": [
        "B"
      ],
      "explanation": {
        "en": "Following the counting convention in the official solution, opposite traversal directions are counted separately. There are 2 cycles of length 3: ADEA and AEDA; 2 of length 4: ABCEA and AECBA; and 2 of length 5: ABCEDA and ADECBA. Total: $2+2+2=6$. Answer B.",
        "zh": "答案：**B**。\n\n按原解析口径，起点固定为 A，同一个环的两个方向分别计数。三边环是 ADEA 与 AEDA；四边环是 ABCEA 与 AECBA；五边环是 ABCEDA 与 ADECBA。三个环各有两个方向，所以共 6 种。"
      },
