    {
      "id": "q5",
      "number": 5,
      "type": "single",
      "topic": {
        "en": "Graph Theory",
        "zh": "图论"
      },
      "statement": {
        "en": "Identify the starting and ending vertices that can be used for the following graph to be traversable.\n\n{{diagram:elementary-q5-graph}}",
        "zh": "要一笔遍历下图的所有边（每条边恰好经过一次），可以使用哪两个顶点作为起点和终点？\n\n{{diagram:elementary-q5-graph}}"
      },
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": {
            "en": "GJ",
            "zh": "GJ"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": {
            "en": "DG",
            "zh": "DG"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": {
            "en": "JD",
            "zh": "JD"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": {
            "en": "Any of them",
            "zh": "任意两个顶点"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "E",
          "text": {
            "en": "None of them",
            "zh": "以上都不可以"
          }
        }
      ],
      "correctOptionIds": [
        "A"
      ],
      "explanation": {
        "en": "For an Euler trail in a connected graph, either 0 or 2 vertices have odd degree. Here the degrees are C=2, D=4, E=2, F=2, G=3, H=2 and J=3. The two odd-degree vertices, G and J, must be the endpoints. Answer A.",
        "zh": "答案：**A**。\n\n一次走过每条边时，经过中间顶点需要一进一出，所用的边成对。图中只有 G、J 的度数是奇数（都为 3），其他顶点都是偶数。因此起点和终点必须是 G 和 J。"
      },
